# Vandeta ucmitm payload - see what the network is doing, without a password.
#
# Two phases, both readable on the run screen and over USB:
#
#   1. `sniff 12`: the clients of the picked AP (802.11 headers are in the clear
#      even on WPA2) and the SSIDs their probe requests are looking for;
#   2. the twin: a neutral notice page, so every client that lands on it reveals
#      the domains it visits - the twin is its DNS server, so the names are read
#      at the source.
#
# `deauth off`: a recon run watches, it does not push anybody off their network.
# Turn it on only when the twin must actually be adopted by clients. If the
# twin cannot start at all, the run still watches the air and reports the
# stations and the SSIDs they are seeking.
#
#   MITM Attack > ucmitm: on > Network > pick the AP > Payload > recon.ucmitm

# A twin SSID of its own: a recon run must never look like the real network, so
# no client roams onto it by accident while it is being watched.
twin Vandeta-Rec
deauth off
sniff 12
page * html/network-notice.html
dns * this
